//! The `columns` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property sets the maximum number of columns to use when drawing an element's contents, along with
//! the minimum width and maximum height of the element's columns.
//!
//! Initial: column-width: auto; column-count: auto; column-height: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The width depends on the values of other properties.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <'column-width'> || <'column-count'> ] [ / <'column-height'> ]?
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-multicol-2/#propdef-columns
